import Wikipedia.HopfProblem.HolomorphicMeromorphicPolarGluingConclusions

/-!
# Native line-bundle gluing of genuine local polar presentations

The imported construction derives actual holomorphic transition units from
the local denominator ideals, proves their cocycle and numerator identities,
and constructs the native line bundle with its holomorphic numerator and
denominator sections. Full chart coordinates recover the given meromorphic
section. A nonempty base has a nonzero denominator section, and native scalar
proportionality of the two sections implies equality with a genuine constant
meromorphic section.

The existence of a cover by local principal presentations is deliberately
separate: it is not assumed to follow from an unproved coherence theorem.
-/
